Track 1: Telescopes Swallow the Saltwater
- Story & Context: Mateo Cruz dragged a dual-spool projector and a brass refractor telescope to the tarred roof of Cine Miramar, intending to track solar flares across the bay before a sudden circuit blowout ignited the blank acetate into a ribbon of caramel-scented fire. Below on the sand, sunbathers cheered at the blinding magenta abstract forms dancing across the sea-cliffs, prompting Mateo to thrust his spit-dampened alto sax into an experimental stutter-pedal to keep time with the melting 24-frame mechanism. The rooftop crowd gathered around the smoking spools, humming the improvised line Mateo belted into his horn: "We only burn what we cannot broadcast."
